## HOLDS (carried; named changes)
- **Kintsugi ONLY.** No tag, rsync, build, swap, probe, login or read on demo. Say so in STATUS A, STATUS B and the HANDOVER. Never production. Never share demo's wallet mnemonic with Kintsugi (KS-535).
- No write on Kintsugi beyond the deploy itself (plus the card-1006 build-cache clear only if the DISK PLAN needs it, carried). **Phase 2's env-file edit, the `.pre-<tag>` copy and the recreates are writes that happen ONLY after the GO ROTATE.** No database stopped (postgres is never touched), no credential created, rotated, revealed or printed in Phase 1; in Phase 2 exactly ONE credential is created and rotated: Redis's. No login to any app, no minted token, no role change.
- **The secret never appears in: a command line you type, an `echo`, a mail, a note, a log, a heredoc, a brief, an evidence file, a history entry, the HANDOVER or a screenshot.** It is generated and consumed on the box. `docker compose config`, `docker inspect` without a name-only format, `env`, `printenv`, `cat` of any env file and `docker logs` of the OLD gateway are FORBIDDEN (they print it). When a command's output might include it, pipe through a mask first and test with a positive control that the mask fires.
- Stop-and-mail on: a REVISION head other than `fab4edcdcd07` (carried; Kintsugi may have moved: re-read at ITEM 0); a Phase 0 prior or idfp mismatch; a build failure (root cause, re-verify, never skip); a gate NOT EQUAL; free disk under 60,000 MB before the build (after the one card-1006 clear) or under 45,000 MB at any point (carried: free was 85,704 MB at k34's end); a migration or tracker mismatch (tracker 59, max 058); a KS-535 value other than `695d09df873ff42b` on anchoring or nft-certificate, a DEMO value present, or (Phase 1) anchoring's StartedAt changed; a REBUILT set other than STATUS A's; a pin that is not the GO's; **the NEW gateway's boot line showing a password, the unmasked shape or no line (PHASE 1 verification item 2)**; any WRONGPASS storm after a Phase 2 step; a signature-class decision (pause for Wednesday).
- Wrap at your context limit (finish the item at ~70%, HANDOVER, wrap at ~75%). A Phase 2 half-done at your limit is the one thing NOT to leave: finish the swap to a consistent state (all clients and Redis on one password) or roll back to the old, then wrap.

## STATUS A (what you send first)
Kintsugi's read-only ITEM 0 (REVISION head, priors, running ids, free disk, KS-535, tracker, binds) since D 71st's FINAL (carried, 2026-11-17 05:12Z); the derived service set at the proposed pin with the gateway's PR list; the H1 measurements that need no log read; the rotation measurements that need no secret (items 1, 2, 4, 5, 7: names, counts and hashes); the throwaway-Redis test result (Q2); the plan; STATUS 2 (before any swap, the nonfinal gate and rollback tag verified). Mail to Wednesday; wait for her GO. The GO names Seat D 72nd and the pin.

## THE GO (what Wednesday sends; PHASE 1 only)
`GO KINTSUGI (Seat D 72nd): pin <sha>.` Plan and STATUS A confirmed. Deploy work (rsync, Phase 0 rollback tag, build, swap) on Kintsugi ONLY at that pin starts on the mail. Usage gate re-read before the build: 98% or more is a STOP before building; once swapping, finish safely. Later merges continue and you ignore them; a pin not reachable in your clone, or a checkout not at that sha, is a STOP and a QUESTION; never substitute a newer tip. THEN, separately, `GO ROTATE (Seat D 72nd)` after she reads STATUS B; with it she rules W4 and W5 and names the sequence.

